(1) A respondent to an appeal may cross appeal any decision on which it could have commenced an appeal, by filing a notice of cross appeal under rule 14.11 .
[How to start a cross appeal]
(2) Subject to subrule (3), where an appeal has been commenced as of right or with permission, the respondent does not need permission to file a cross appeal with respect to any decision described in rule 14.5 [Appeals only with permission] if the cross appeal is only intended to vary the decision already under appeal.
(3) Where an enactment provides that an appeal may be commenced in the Court of Appeal with permission, a respondent who wishes to cross appeal must apply for permission to cross appeal.
